### Project Description — Automated Specification Upload to Cognia Knowledge Bases

This n8n workflow automates the synchronization of BRS (Business Requirements Specification), SRS (Software Requirements Specification), and SDS (Software Design Specification) documents from the GitHub `dnext-product-docs` repository to their respective Cognia Knowledge Bases.

The workflow detects relevant document changes, retrieves Markdown files, identifies the appropriate Knowledge Base, and uploads documents through authenticated REST API requests using Keycloak OAuth2.

To prevent duplicate uploads, it checks previously successful uploads in the audit table before processing each document. It also records upload results, handles errors, and tracks processing status.

**Key Features:**
- Automated GitHub change detection and document retrieval
- Dynamic routing to BRS, SRS, and SDS Knowledge Bases
- Secure authentication through Keycloak OAuth2
- Sequential document processing using n8n loops
- Duplicate upload prevention through audit history
- Upload status logging and error handling
- Commit tracker updates only after successful processing of all relevant documents

**Goal:** Maintain reliable, traceable, and automated synchronization between GitHub specification documents and Cognia Knowledge Bases while minimizing manual effort and duplicate uploads.
